[Music]  how much of civilization is shaped by  our biology  how might our cities transportation and  technology look different if we weren't  a group of nearly hairless primates  the video game spore has the answers  okay well maybe not the answers but  spore does offer an interesting case  study into the fundamentals of how a  speculative life form might build a  society  in our first war episode we followed a  life form from a microscopic organism to  the intelligent curiosis sapiens  in this episode we'll witness the ascent  of their civilization and explore how  the unique biology of an alien like  curiosis sapiens would affect things  like the design of clothing the  schematics of vehicles and the shapes of  buildings in unexpected ways we'll begin  with tribal stage and go all the way to  space completing the multi-billion year  tale of curiosis sapiens  so let's return to planet curious and  discover the finale of the story of life  after the early evolutionary stages the  birth of society is underway with  curiosis sapiens building fires in early  lodgings  but is this the dawn of a wise people or  a culture of warmongering tyrants what  path will curiosis sapiens take in  shaping the destiny of their planet  like the game's biology cultural  evolution and spore is fairly simplified  and exaggerated tribal stage seems to be  a mesh of various eras but seems most  comparable to a hunter-gatherer culture  at this point in history curiosis  sapiens appear to only have access to  simple technologies quite similar to  that of early humans  it might seem surprising that  curiosities would converge on concepts  like pottery but there is some precedent  for this idea  on earth certain technologies are  cultural universals meaning that  numerous cultures invented a version of  them independently from one another the  sheer number of times disparate  populations have invented something like  pottery indicates that when intelligent  minds are faced with the same problem  similar answers might emerge whether or  not this would hold true for an alien in  an alien environment is difficult to say  but depending on the circumstances  curiosis sapiens inventing pottery is  certainly possible  as technology improves spore gives us  the option to determine the clothing of  curiosity sapiens the question of what  kind of clothes an emerging sapient  alien species would wear assuming they'd  wear clothing at all is actually a  tricky one clothing is so ubiquitous  today for us homo sapiens that we almost  don't think about it the initial  invention of clothing was likely tied to  climate and served as a way to protect  our hairless bodies from the elements  yet compared to earth planet curious  like most planets in spore seems to have  an extremely temperate macro climate so  it's unlikely clothing would develop  from temperature control alone yet  clothing can also protect the body from  specific environmental hazards like  pests abrasive substances and other  irritants so it's possible that  protective attire would first emerge in  curiosis sapiens in particularly  vulnerable areas like the base of their  eyestalks  human clothing also has various social  functions across cultures and some  articles of alien clothing could serve  in these ways unlike humans curiosis  sapiens have an elaborate display  structure sprouting from their shoulders  similar to the extravagant plumages of  certain birds it's not too big a leap to  assume garments would be built around  complementing these structures making  them appear fuller and more impressive  an emergent hunter-gatherer species  would also likely find value in various  satchels or pouches to carry resources  and finally aliens might develop some  articles of clothing with no apparent  function whatsoever either as  reflections of cultural trends or  expressions of personal style  in the case of curiosities clothing  choices would be limited by available  materials which in this age would likely  comprise hides grass leaves and shells  the end result is a tire that certainly  looks pretty strange to our eyes but a  curiosity sapiens would likely find the  eccentricities of our clothing just as  puzzling  as time passes curiosis sapiens fall  into a rhythm within the hunter-gatherer  lifestyle with obtaining food the most  important task during this era  historically permanent settlements on  earth rarely emerge until after the  invention of agriculture and  domesticated plants spore skips over any  mention of agriculture but realistically  we can assume that curiosities have some  early version of subsistence farming  figured out in curiosis sapiens aren't  the only life forms to have achieved  advanced intelligence across planet  curious other species are building their  own societies different unrelated  species reaching the same level of  technological advancement during the  exact same period isn't particularly  likely but this is how spore functions  the question is how will curiosis  sapiens choose to interact with their  new neighbors going forwards  to guide curiosis sapiens through this  new era two tools are now available for  construction the spear and the wooden  horn which looks like a kind of  rudimentary flute as far as early tools  go these are actually fairly plausible  spears are the oldest weapon we have an  unambiguous archaeological record of  dating back to the paleolithic age  likewise mammoth bone flutes from the  paleolithic are the oldest known musical  instruments realistically however the  tools of a species like curiosis sapiens  would likely be different from our own  for one since curiosis sapiens only have  four fingers instead of five their  musical instruments would likely look  different as they'd probably only have  access to a pentatonic scale instead of  a heptatonic one when playing a wind  instrument with five notes per octave  instead of seven  likewise it's interesting to deliberate  on whether a life form like curiosis  sapiens would develop a spear in the  first place humans lack the claws and  fangs of most top predators in the  animal kingdom pressuring early humans  to invent tools to compete with the  natural weaponry of other animals yet an  unarmed curiosity sapiens is already a  formidable customer and might not need  to be as creative  still it's possible that any emergent  tool user would be able to puzzle out  the basic concept that sticking  something sharp on the end of something  long is a good way to deal damage while  keeping yourself out of harm's reach in  either case with their new tools  curiosis sapiens can now enchant other  species with their musical instruments  or impale them on the end of their spear  as thinking social omnivores curiosis  sapiens make allies when they can but  when another species attacks first  curiosis sapiens respond in kind in a  trend that sadly echoes our own history  this early era is marked by frequent  conflict  but society is also changing in other  ways curiosity sapiens are on the path  towards creating a larger and more  stable civilization a path laden with  new developments at this point curiosity  sapiens gain the ability to domesticate  animals a crucial trait for emergent  civilizations there's a lot that could  be said about animal domestication but  to simplify we humans began our animal  domestication journey with wolves before  the agricultural revolution then moved  on to small herbivores like sheep and  goats once we began staying in one place  for longer beasts of burden that could  plow fields or give you a ride like cows  and horses came later curiosis sapiens  will begin their journey with this small  bird-like quadruped harvesting their  feathers for clothing and construction  materials in their eggs for dietary  consumption generations later the second  animal curiosis sapiens domesticate is  this large horrifying spider beast these  hearty giants might look intimidating  but they're actually quite docile and  will fill the role of plow animals it's  worth noting that while once again spore  never touches on agriculture in order  for this sort of domestication to be  possible curioso sapiens must have begun  the practice and with these animals in  their corner the population can grow to  new sizes and society itself can become  more complex  new buildings are now available like  this outlet for fishing spears  seemingly implying the emergence of  small industries and the increased  specialization of tasks within curiosa  sapiens society and just looking at  their society culture seems richer and  more diverse with different curiosity  sapiens sharing ideas and playing  musical instruments after making one  final alliance spore gives us the option  to advance to the next stage  hurtling forwards in time civilization  stage begins with the option to build a  modern building once again spore's  timeline of historical change is  certainly a simplified one as there are  historically numerous steps between  small subsistence societies in an  emergent industrial civilization  likewise spore puts no limits on this  first building letting you construct  something truly absurd if you feel like  it fun as that can be it's interesting  to consider what an early industrial  house might look like for curiosis  sapiens unlike humans curiosis sapiens  are nest builders and have been for the  past several hundred million years of  their evolution as a result it's  possible that their instincts for houses  would be different from our own building  smaller more low to the ground dwellings  that evoke their ancestral nests  with a town hall constructed the  curiosity sapiens debate the nature of  their society  with a stable food supply natural  resources like spice which flows from  most planets in spore becomes the new  valued commodity the value of spice and  spore reminds me of the sci-fi world  dune and if my memory of that series is  accurate a reliance on spice might cause  problems but for now curios's sapiens  are a young populace with their heads  lost in the dream of the future  on that note spore gives us the option  to design our first vehicle that will  help with transporting the spice as  always spore lets you design whatever  absurd thing you want but alien cars  genuinely might not look like what we'd  expect  certain things like wheels could be  universal considering the constraints of  physics yet our vehicles reflect us more  than we realize  several studies have shown that when we  look at most cars our brain's facial  recognition cortex is activated this  isn't a coincidence cars are designed to  subtly resemble human faces to appeal to  our pattern-seeking minds and if  curiosis sapiens have similar instincts  it's likely their vehicles would subtly  reflect the geometry of their faces  with the first vehicle constructed the  spice can be gathered and transported  for better or worse in this era other  civilizations of curiosities have also  emerged we've already seen this species  much like humans has the potential for  war and cooperation so the ultimate  future of planet curious will be  determined by how well they can work  together contacting our closest  neighbors we can offer gifts compliment  them or say their people are descended  from limless space slugs now i'm no  political expert but i suspect one of  the first two options is a better tactic  thanks to such savvy political acumen  the two civilizations establish a trade  route and begin the long road towards a  united future as time passes cities  become larger and full of new  technologies thanks to the steady force  of negotiation alliances form first with  immediate neighbors and then with more  distant countries as technology improves  clothing evolves as well featuring new  textiles and construction materials i  tried to make the post-industrial  clothes of curiosis sapiens still  vaguely echo earlier cultural trends got  to keep those silly hats after all  in time we unlock the secrets of  motorized flying machines and can design  our first air vehicles here the  constraints of things like wind  resistance might shape our craft into  something similar to the planes we have  on earth although just like with their  land vehicles curiosis sapiens may build  something that subtly reflects the  geometry of their faces and with their  natural stock eyes and more flexible  necks curiosity sapiens likely have a  greater visual field than humans so the  cockpits of their aircrafts might have  more windows to the sides and back  with aircrafts now soaring through the  atmosphere the planet is more connected  through trade than ever before achieving  planetary peace through careful  management and negotiation is admittedly  not the most exciting but it's certainly  worth it  at the end of this era  sapiens are united under one banner and  looking towards the stars as their next  horizon  and so the final chapter space stage  begins curiosis sapiens are no longer  beholden to just a single meager world  after designing a spacecraft that  follows the same aesthetic standards of  other vehicles for the first time  curiosis sapiens are free to explore  beyond the protective atmosphere of  their home  traveling to another planet in the  system the sapiens discover a crash  vessel and are lucky enough to scan and  replicate its interstellar drive  from the perspective of the player you  can now zoom out and behold the entire  galaxy spinning just like how it is in  the title screen except you can now go  to any part of it you like that first  moment when you realize the whole galaxy  is now yours to explore is pretty  magical and makes the scope of spore  feel so impossibly vast the galaxy is  waiting and the rest is up to you  every one of these stars contains their  own system of orbiting planets which you  can fly down to and visit at the time  when spore first came out this kind of  procedurally generated universe was  something never really attempted before  at the same time such scale has its  drawbacks it's hard not to feel like in  a galaxy this large nothing you do has  much meaning i know a lot of people's  least favorite stage is space stage and  i understand why it's easy to become  disconnected from the creature you  started with billions of years ago  although perhaps that's an unavoidable  symptom of a species becoming a galaxy  spanning civilization  expanding across the cosmos curiosis  sapiens gain the ability to build  self-assembling colonies on barren  worlds in their expansion they search  for radio wave frequencies that might  signal the presence of technologically  advanced life like themselves on our  planet we're scanning the stars for  alien life by searching for similar  frequencies although with our limited  range so far we've found nothing but  silence yet curiosity sapiens can  journey much further out across the  stars and eventually they encounter  other intelligent space-faring life who  rose from the primordial soup just like  they did in time curios's sapiens even  unlock the secrets of life and can  create creatures to populate newly  terraformed worlds this kind of power  can be used to create bizarre forms of  life as biology becomes an infinite  playground in the words of science  fiction author arthur c clarke any  sufficiently advanced technology is  indistinguishable from magic and that  adage holds true here it can also be  used more responsibly and we'd have to  hope that such an advanced form of life  would be sensible with their power  looking forwards curiosis sapiens will  ascend to a civilization we can't fathom  transcending technology beyond the scope  of our limited minds  by design spore skips over many of the  stages of history condensing and  exaggerating the long road of  technological advancement yet the game  does explore a surprising number of the  universal principles of how  civilizations and technology change over  time i know not everybody likes the  later stages of spore compared to cell  and creature and i can understand that  still the novelty of guiding a  speculative creature through their  technological advancement is still  pretty intriguing even all these years  later like i said in part 1 i'd love to  see another high profile game tackle  something similar as i feel there's real  potential for a modern take on this  concept  as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support to help make videos like this  possible by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious see you in  the next video  i

